## 💡 Why this works better for advanced filters
Some security filters use a generic "catch-all" block that checks your entire HTTP request. If you fill multiple boxes with script inputs simultaneously, you might trigger an aggressive web application firewall block.
By injecting into only one single parameter at a time while leaving everything else looking normal, you look like a standard user registering or logging in, which increases the likelihood of finding raw inputs that bypass poorly configured validation logic.
